From 8848208d5490053b0fab87695dc3b27a5c7f70db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:09:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] annotation host copy: holder demand per profile,
 renew before expiry, disk copy v2
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Follow-ups from independent review 5891094785 (card t_01a1d4e06d3fd78b) of PR #2200
(annotation host copy, design t_01a1d45d75851804 §2c). Card t_01a1d4e905dd65c1.

1. `_holder_pass` read `_disk.demand_age(scope)` outside `ctx.run`, so `_path()`
   (`get_hermes_home()`) looked for a non-launch profile's demand file under the
   launch home: in a serve hosting several profiles the holder never refreshed
   those scopes. The demand check now runs in `_holder_refresh`, inside the
   scope's own context.
2. The holder's re-read at HOLDER_REFRESH_AGE_S (20 s) was a counts-cache hit
   while the inputs stayed revalidatable, so publish rewrote the same `read_at`
   every 2 s and the copy only renewed when the cache expired at 30 s, leaving a
   window where adopters missed. When the copy has aged past the renew threshold
   the holder sets `_revalidate.force_read.scope`, which makes `counts_fresh`
   refuse the cache for that scope on that thread, so a real read publishes a
   fresh `read_at` before adopters drop the copy.
3. `kanban_annotation_disk._VERSION` 1 -> 2: the restart/host copy encoding now
   wraps lists/dicts as {l}/{d}; an older core would have seeded those wrappers
   as data for one cold start. v1 copies are now ignored (one cold start).

Tests (RED before, GREEN after):
- test_holder_refreshes_a_scope_demanded_on_another_profile (0 == 1 before)
- test_holder_renews_the_copy_before_adopters_would_miss (max copy age 30.0
  before; <= 22 s after, and an adopter adopts at the end)
- test_a_version_1_copy_is_ignored
11 annotation/session-activity test files: 167 passed. scripts/check ok.
